Protected members are different. A protected member is accessible within the same package and is also accessible to subclasses outside the package through inheritance.

For example, if Parent and Child are in different packages, Child can directly access a protected member inherited from Parent, but it cannot access that member through an arbitrary Parent object reference.

Default, or package-private, members are accessible only within the same package, so a subclass in a different package cannot access them.

